      "DANIELS: The crew is made up of couples. That was the whole point ... Everyone but me now.\nDANIELS: I thought you might know something about being alone.\nFARIS: Hey, Danny.\nDANIELS: Thanks for coming.",
      "FARIS: God damn. It’s just like Earth...\nDANIELS: We’ll see, right?\nFARIS: What I wouldn’t give to feel a little ocean breeze, catch me some waves...",
      "UPWORTH: Everything looking good down there?\nFARIS: All good, Covenant. Expect to hit upper atmosphere in five ... Might want to hang on in the back, we’re about to--\nFARIS: Covenant? You read us?",
      "UPWORTH: - LANDER, DO YOU READ!?\nFARIS: Yeah, yeah. I read you. Think we’re... OK now.\nFARIS: Underway - looks like we got mountains.",
      "FARIS: New power cells must have fritzed out. I’ll cycle ‘em while you’re gone.\nDANIELS: How far out are we?"
